<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" name="Each IG, composed into a host docs site and rendered with just-the-docs" processRef="Process_IgDocsSiteCompose"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" name="Each IG, composed into a host docs site and rendered with just-the-docs" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>How a host docs site builds every IG it mounts INSIDE itself, so each IG's pages wear the host's chrome (one sidebar, one search, one language selector) rather than being a site of their own (bean `mftp`, owner 2026-10-05: "Build in main site"). This is the `stage-ig-sites` Tool's own subprocess: a host's general publish process reaches it through a Tool-bound step that names `docs-generation` (in cat-harness's `docs-site-publish`, `Call_InstanceSites`), and the Tool's `subprocesses` point here.

NO IG PUBLISHER RUNS. The IG's source (`sushi-config.yaml`, `input/pagecontent`, `input/includes`, `input/images`, `input/data`) is turned into Jekyll source by `build-ig-site`, with the Publisher's `site.data.fhir` filled from the IG's AST and its `sushi-config.yaml`, and the host's ONE Jekyll build renders it with just-the-docs (skill `ig-render-jekyll`). Which IGs is DATA: each instance whose `fhir-artifact-index/menu.json` records a `source.of` (the IG repository) and `source.ref` (the commit). No workflow and no step here names an IG.

THE STEPS AND THEIR TOOLS, in the order a host runs them: `ig-index-build` (`bun run cat ig-index:build`) writes each IG instance's `fhir-artifact-index/`; `ig-pages` (`gen-ig-pages.ts`, run per instance by that instance's own `&lt;instance&gt;:pages` script) writes its artefact pages; `stage-ig-sites` clones each IG at its recorded commit and stages it with `build-ig-site`; with `--compose-into` it moves each staged site into the host's Jekyll source at `&lt;instance&gt;/`. The host then builds, and runs this Tool's post-build pass, `build-ig-site --dedupe-ids`, over each composed IG's built pages. In folio-assistant's `docs-site.yml` the first two steps run before the release security gate, because the QA working copy reads what they write; they are drawn here because they are this Tool's inputs.

`feature-staging.yml` runs the same steps for a pull request's preview, with `--changed-files`, so only the IGs a change reaches are rebuilt (bean `4j86`). An IG repository building its OWN site runs `stage-ig-sites --only &lt;instance&gt; --source &lt;checkout&gt;` instead, which is `ig-ast-cache`'s `Task_BuildSite`, not this process.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <!-- ADVISORY: a drawing of what docs-site.yml already runs. Strict would
           bind a host to these steps by name, when a host with no IG
           instance has none to run. -->
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="advisory"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Build" name="Host docs site build (CI runner)">
        <bpmn:documentation>The host's publish or preview job: GitHub Actions running each Tool's command in one runner. Mechanical throughout: it decides nothing a person must own, and it reports rather than guesses. An instance with no recorded source is skipped and named, never silently absent, and a theme it cannot choose between is refused.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="build-pipeline"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Compose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Indexes</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Pages</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Stage</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ComposeInto</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Composed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Compose" name="Host docs source&#10;composed; IG sites&#10;wanted">
      <bpmn:documentation>The host has composed its docs layers into one Jekyll source (`compose-docs --out ./_docs`) and the IG instances are on disk (`bun run cat state:mount` lays down the remote mounts from the lock).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Indexes" name="Build each IG's&#10;artefact index&#10;[ig-index-build]">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `ig-index-build`: `bun run cat ig-index:build` (`fhir-harness/scripts/build-ig-indexes.ts`). For each IG instance (one that needs this layer, declares a `repository`, and whose repository carries an AST branch family) it restores the AST from the IG repository's cache branch (`ig-cache.sh restore`) and writes `fhir-artifact-index/`: `index.json` from the AST, `menu.json` from the IG's `sushi-config.yaml` at the commit cloned (recording `source.of` and `source.ref`, which `Task_Stage` clones from), `releases.json` from the repository's GitHub releases, and `package.tgz` from the AST's resources. A missing input skips that instance and the run says which and why.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ig-build-pipeline"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Pages" name="Generate each IG&#10;instance's artefact&#10;pages [ig-pages]">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `ig-pages`: `bun run fhir-harness/scripts/gen-ig-pages.ts --instance &lt;instance&gt; ...`, run by each IG instance's own pages script (in folio-assistant, `bun run smart:pages`, then `smart:pages:publish`, which also writes the OpenAPI pages). It writes `&lt;instance&gt;/docs/` from the artefact index: one thin page per artefact with its JSON-LD node beside it, and, for an instance whose docs declare `igSite`, only a front-matter `artifacts.md`, because the IG site's own index, menu and category pages replace the rest. These pages are built at publish and never committed by the IG's fork.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ig-build-pipeline"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Stage" name="Clone each IG at its&#10;recorded commit and&#10;stage it [stage-ig-sites]">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `stage-ig-sites`, which calls Tool `build-ig-site` once per IG: `bun run fhir-harness/scripts/stage-ig-sites.ts --work ./_ig --baseurl /&lt;repo&gt; --plantuml-jar &lt;jar&gt;`. For every instance holding `fhir-artifact-index/menu.json` with a sushi-config source, it clones `source.of` at `source.ref` and stages ONE Jekyll source for just-the-docs: `input/pagecontent/*.md` as pages with title, parent and order from `sushi-config.yaml` `pages:`; `input/includes`, `input/pagecontent` and `input/images/*.svg` as `_includes/`; `input/images/**` at the site root; `input/images-source/*.plantuml` rendered to SVG with the PlantUML jar (else a visible "not rendered" marker); the Publisher's generated artefact lists as Liquid over the index; `_data/fhir.json` from `ig-site-data`; `input/data/*` as `_data/`; and the colour scheme of the one `webpage` theme the instance declares or inherits along `needs` (two at the same distance are refused). The instance's artefact pages from `Task_Pages` are copied in.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ig-render-jekyll"/>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ig-build-pipeline"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ComposeInto" name="Compose each staged&#10;IG into the host source&#10;[stage-ig-sites]">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tool `stage-ig-sites` with `--compose-into ./_docs` (the same run as `Task_Stage`). Each staged site moves INTO the host's Jekyll source at `&lt;instance&gt;/`, with its includes and data namespaced per IG, so the host's own Jekyll build renders it. Pages wear the thin layout with the host's chrome linked, not inlined (the default since 2026-10-12; `--full-pages` builds the earlier full pages). The run prints one `&lt;instance&gt; &lt;jekyll source&gt; &lt;at&gt;` line per IG, the build list the host keeps (`./_ig-list.txt`) for the post-build pass.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ig-render-jekyll"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Composed" name="Each IG composed;&#10;build list handed&#10;to the host">
      <bpmn:documentation>The host's Jekyll source now holds every IG, and the build list names them. The host builds it ONCE (`bundle exec jekyll build --source ./_docs --destination ./_site`, Jekyll 4 with `jekyll-remote-theme` loading just-the-docs), then runs this Tool's post-build pass for each line of the list: Tool `build-ig-site` with `--dedupe-ids ./_site/&lt;instance&gt;`, which keeps the first copy of an anchor the IG's source repeats (where every link already lands), renames the rest, and reports each one.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Start_Compose" targetRef="Task_Indexes"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="Task_Indexes" targetRef="Task_Pages"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="Task_Pages" targetRef="Task_Stage"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="Task_Stage" targetRef="Task_ComposeInto"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="Task_ComposeInto" targetRef="End_Composed"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_IgDocsSiteCompose" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="60" width="1300" height="200" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Build" bpmnElement="Lane_Build" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="90" y="60" width="1270" height="200" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Compose" bpmnElement="Start_Compose"><dc:Bounds x="152" y="142" width="36" height="36" /><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="110" y="184" width="120" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Indexes" bpmnElement="Task_Indexes"><dc:Bounds x="260" y="110" width="160" height="100" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Pages" bpmnElement="Task_Pages"><dc:Bounds x="490" y="110" width="160" height="100" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Stage" bpmnElement="Task_Stage"><dc:Bounds x="720" y="110" width="160" height="100" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_ComposeInto" bpmnElement="Task_ComposeInto"><dc:Bounds x="950" y="110" width="160" height="100" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Composed" bpmnElement="End_Composed"><dc:Bounds x="1212" y="142" width="36" height="36" /><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1170" y="184" width="120" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_1" bpmnElement="Flow_1"><di:waypoint x="188" y="160" /><di:waypoint x="260" y="160" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_2" bpmnElement="Flow_2"><di:waypoint x="420" y="160" /><di:waypoint x="490" y="160" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_3" bpmnElement="Flow_3"><di:waypoint x="650" y="160" /><di:waypoint x="720" y="160" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_4" bpmnElement="Flow_4"><di:waypoint x="880" y="160" /><di:waypoint x="950" y="160" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_5" bpmnElement="Flow_5"><di:waypoint x="1110" y="160" /><di:waypoint x="1212" y="160" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
